 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met. By the code's count, four of the five cases cleared the bar: 096988dd with cars shifted +2 s at 1.25x speed (S11), 023b7fcc at \u22122 s and 1.5x (S2), 19f339ba at \u22120.5 s and 1.5x (S28), and 1c45ce3a at 0 s and 0.75x (S32). Each has only a few repeats, so the true failure rate is only known to be above one half. Triage of the videos and logs shows that only two of these four are failures by the policy. In S11 and S28 the policy drifted left into the next lane and hit a car driving alongside, even at 2 Hz planning. S2's failures are rear contacts that began before the policy took over. S32's are a replayed car cutting in and clipping the ego, which stayed in its lane. One more scene, 09a95ffa at 0 s and 1.25x (S12), also shows the policy's left drift, but its failure rate was not shown to be above one half.",
